WEBVTT

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:05.240
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:10.260
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:15.540
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:33.290
Pikachu! It’s going your way!

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:44.980
Are you okay, Messon?

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:46.900
H-Hey...

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:53.470
Messon... C’mon, cheer up.

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:56.800
Hihidaruma takes any chance it gets
to play a prank...

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:58.710
You might want to hit back
every now and then!

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:04.980
Well, Messon will be Messon...

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:07.660
Oh, it was incredible!

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:11.180
When I went out for lunch, they were shooting a movie
in the warehouse district!

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:15.010
And get this, it was the sequel
to “Spy & Sniper”!

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:17.680
Really?! That’s a big title!

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:20.430
What’s that?

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:21.680
You don’t know it?!

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:25.710
It’s a movie starring a
female spy Pokémon Trainer,

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:28.820
and she has this really cool
Inteleon partner!

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:33.480
Inteleon! Agent Pokémon!
Water type!

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.330
Its body has many
hidden capabilities,

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:38.660
such as fingertips
that can shoot water,

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:41.210
and a membrane on its back
that it can use to glide through the air!

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:44.180
It’s a huge hit that keeps people
coming back for more.

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:46.270
Yeah! It does look cool!

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:47.780
Right?

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.970
Looks like even Messon’s interested.

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:54.590
Well, Inteleon <i>is</i>
Messon’s final evolution.

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:57.640
I wanna see it!
Do you think they’re still filming?

00:01:57.640 --> 00:01:58.680
Let’s go see!

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:43.750
And so, Satoshi and Go
have arrived at the film shoot.

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:46.000
According to Renji,
this should be it—

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.970
<i>This</i> is not <i>it!</i>

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:49.490
That voice...!

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:55.380
This man is Director Koreda,
a master of the movie world.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:04:00.880
This isn’t it!

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:07.690
Thanks to Director Sakuragi, Satoshi and Go
were able to watch him film a movie once before.

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:10.990
If this does that, no,
if <i>that</i> does that...

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:12.990
It just needs a bit more flair...

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:18.150
Um... What should we do?
Everyone’s already standing by...

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:22.160
Agh, let’s go for it!

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:24.040
They’re starting, Messon!

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:27.000
Ready, start!

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:33.000
Hand over the case.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.000
Go, Yamikarasu!

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:43.510
Good timing, partner.

00:04:47.770 --> 00:04:49.570
Stop them both!

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:58.320
What?!

00:04:58.320 --> 00:04:59.700
Hold...

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:01.070
...your...

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:02.820
...battle!

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:05.900
We are your aides, meow!

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:08.830
Get in, Inteleon!
We’ll make a getaway.

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:11.960
Um...
Was this in the script?

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:14.980
Who are those cartoonish intruders?!
Stop the came—

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:16.840
Don’t stop the cameras!

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:17.340
Sir?

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:21.720
This may just create <i>that!</i>
Keep filming!

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:32.310
So you’re not gonna fall for
this cliché plot...

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:38.280
If you say “Leo, leo”...

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:41.480
We’ll answer out of
sympathy for the world!

00:05:42.910 --> 00:05:45.380
To protect the world from devastation.

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:48.200
To preserve world peace.

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:51.460
Championing the evils
of truth and love.

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:54.420
We’re the lovely, charming villains.

00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:55.800
Musashi!

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:56.870
Kojiro!

00:05:57.290 --> 00:06:00.630
The Team Rocket duo
soars through the galaxy!

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:03.630
Like a white hole,
a white tomorrow awaits us!

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:06.000
Just kidding, meow!

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:12.550
Team Rocket is on the scene!

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:15.370
Those guys were Team Rocket?!

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:18.300
A third side shows up!

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.230
This is it, this is it, this is it!

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:24.860
Inteleon! We’ve seen what you can do
in your movie.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:30.950
Your sharp mind and spy skills...
We’d love to have you aid Team Rocket!

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:35.590
So there you have it.
Shut up and come with us, meow!

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:36.990
Don’t be so selfish!

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:38.970
We won’t let you
get in the way of the filming!

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:40.940
The brat boys?

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:43.340
We won’t let <i>you</i> get in <i>our</i> way,
either, meow!

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:45.390
Director!
Now there’s <i>more</i> weird intruders...

00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:47.450
Don’t stop the cameras!

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:49.850
Vending, come on!

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:56.840
All right...

00:06:57.650 --> 00:07:00.110
Here goes, meow!

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:02.320
Rocket...

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:03.340
Vending...

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:05.070
Secret!

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:08.300
I wonder, what’ll I get?

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:13.020
The Bite Pokémon,
Poochyena!

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:15.590
Yay!

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:18.880
The Dark Pokémon,
Delvil!

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.750
All right!

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:23.670
Go, Pikachu!

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:25.930
Aceburn, go!

00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:31.350
Poochyena! Um, um, Yawn!

00:07:32.850 --> 00:07:34.160
Dodge it!

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:38.460
Now <i>this</i> is a... movie...

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:41.740
Director!

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:43.570
How could you!

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:45.360
Your fault for dodging.

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:49.540
Hey. It’s that crybaby
Pokémon again.

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:51.010
Oh, so it is.

00:07:57.460 --> 00:08:00.080
Then there’s just one thing to do.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:02.670
Poochyena!
Scary Face the blue thing!

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:11.180
Oh, no!

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:12.680
Yay, yay!

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:15.560
That’s really cruel!

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:18.390
It’s your fault for bringing
that dead weight!

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:19.860
Yeah, that’s right!

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:22.190
Nyahahaha-ha!

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:25.070
Now! Delvil,
use Ember on them!

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:26.900
Poochyena! Shadow Ball!

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:31.280
Inteleon! Snipe Shot.

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:33.240
What?!

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:48.620
When did it...?

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:50.960
Concealing yourself without a sound,
without a trace...

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:53.820
That’s the first rule
of being a spy.

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:55.890
Right, Inteleon?

00:08:57.350 --> 00:08:58.390
It disappeared again?!

00:08:58.390 --> 00:08:59.950
Where’d it go, meow?

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:01.650
Now. Snipe Shot!

00:09:07.990 --> 00:09:09.320
We may have failed...

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:12.520
<i>But that Inteleon gives us
such a great feeling!</i>

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:20.110
Amazing...

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:23.260
We’re wrapping up
the shoot early today!

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:25.750
Please clear the way!

00:09:26.110 --> 00:09:28.020
That Inteleon was awesome!

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:31.920
Yeah! Even Messon
was totally entranced...

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:33.510
Huh? Where’d it go?

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:36.970
Hey! This area is for staff only!

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:40.870
Sorry! That’s my Messon!

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:43.440
You have to keep a close eye
on your Pokémon!

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:46.650
Messon...?

00:09:46.650 --> 00:09:51.210
Um... Messon and I
had never seen an Inteleon before,

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:54.740
so please, is there any chance
we could spend some time with it?

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:56.060
What...?

00:09:56.060 --> 00:09:58.790
That’s fine.
Our schedule cleared up anyway.

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:03.350
You must be happy, Messon!

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:08.520
That brings back memories.
It looks a lot like Inteleon used to.

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:09.920
Really?!

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:14.420
Yes. He was my partner,
even off camera.

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:18.060
Even he wasn’t always this strong.

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:35.700
Great going!

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:38.950
Messon’s really
looking up to Inteleon.

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:44.960
It did it again?!

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:56.330
Getting stronger will take time.

00:10:57.300 --> 00:11:01.930
So what do you think?
Would you like to train with me?

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:11.360
Hah... Inteleon was
every bit as strong as I thought!

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:14.480
All the more reason
we should make it ours, meow.

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:19.320
But with that strength...
Brute force isn’t going to—

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:20.630
All done!

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:22.800
What’s that, meow?

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:24.240
A thorough plan.

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:26.870
Think about the Pokémon we’re taking on.

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:30.500
We’ll need to make
lots of preparations to catch it.

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:33.470
Pocket Monsters!

00:11:43.460 --> 00:11:46.520
All right!
Let’s train with all we’ve got!

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:50.850
Or well... What sort of training
should we even do?

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:53.090
Battling, naturally!

00:11:53.090 --> 00:11:55.560
That Inteleon was super strong!

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:57.560
Well, let’s give it a try.

00:11:59.050 --> 00:12:01.150
Hit us with all you’ve got, okay?

00:12:02.770 --> 00:12:04.670
Okay then,
let’s get started, Messon!

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:07.870
Use Pound on Pikachu!

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:09.810
Counter it, Pikachu!

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:16.380
You’re scared of getting up close?

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:19.890
Then attack from a distance!
Messon! Water Gun!

00:12:21.850 --> 00:12:24.220
If you’re not moving,
you’re gonna get targeted!

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:25.850
Pikachu! Lightning Speed!

00:12:27.310 --> 00:12:29.570
Messon! Fire while dodging!

00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:34.000
Where’s the Water Gun?

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:38.490
I think... It prioritizes protecting itself
rather than fighting back.

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:42.110
It’s a hundred percent focused on
fleeing right now...

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:44.910
Well, staying safe is staying safe...

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:47.120
But that’s not much of a battle.

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:48.660
Let’s take a break!

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:58.420
Maybe Messon just
isn’t cut out for this.

00:13:00.680 --> 00:13:04.240
Oh, that’s not it!
I meant your battle style.

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:11.020
Messon, you always watch your surroundings carefully,
and run away at the slightest danger, right?

00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:17.650
People may call you timid,
but I think it’s good to protect yourself!

00:13:19.100 --> 00:13:22.860
But that trait isn’t something
normal methods take advantage of...

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:26.750
We need another way.
Something that puts your timidness to good use.

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:30.430
Puts timidness to good use?

00:13:30.430 --> 00:13:33.290
You mean, something like
running and hiding?

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:36.660
No, that won’t help battle...

00:13:37.520 --> 00:13:38.550
Maybe it will!

00:13:38.550 --> 00:13:39.330
Huh?

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:42.200
Concealing yourself without a sound,
without a trace...

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:44.080
That’s the first rule
of being a spy.

00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:46.390
We’ll hone your skills of
running and hiding!

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:50.540
Let’s play tag, like a spy!

00:13:50.540 --> 00:13:55.080
We’ll all chase you, while you run around
and try to avoid capture!

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:57.270
That’s great! It sounds fun!

00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:59.940
Aceburn, you help out too!

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:05.110
Ready... Start!

00:14:08.130 --> 00:14:09.710
Hold it!

00:14:11.190 --> 00:14:12.650
Pikachu, go for it!

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:22.660
Messon spotted!

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:27.850
I feel like it should be around here...

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:39.530
Gotta do better! One more time!

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:44.010
Where’d it go?

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:47.490
Maybe over there?

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:53.040
Here!

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:54.340
It went that way!

00:15:01.990 --> 00:15:04.010
Messon looked like it had fun!

00:15:04.010 --> 00:15:05.710
It was getting better and better.

00:15:07.100 --> 00:15:10.380
Somebody, help!

00:15:11.870 --> 00:15:13.520
Are you okay?

00:15:13.520 --> 00:15:14.940
You’re from that film crew!

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:18.270
I went with Gothim
to get lunch for everyone...

00:15:22.030 --> 00:15:25.570
One hostage kidnapped!
Or rather, Pokénapped!

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:29.070
If you want it back...

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:32.200
They said I’d have to
bring Inteleon to this spot...

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:33.650
Those creeps...

00:15:33.650 --> 00:15:35.810
So they hadn’t given up on him yet?!

00:15:35.810 --> 00:15:37.210
We’ll go on ahead!

00:15:37.210 --> 00:15:39.370
You go let everyone know
what happened!

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:40.540
Got it!

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:45.770
It’s probably around here...

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:52.530
Let’s go.

00:15:55.150 --> 00:15:59.640
I was surprised to see a cave
with so much built in it...

00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:02.190
But what are those things?

00:16:04.890 --> 00:16:06.650
I thought they could be lookouts,

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:09.950
but they’re not
attacking us or anything...

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:13.520
And they seem to be placed all over...

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:17.910
Well, if they’re not getting in the way,
let’s go find Gothim.

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:18.960
Right.

00:16:21.340 --> 00:16:22.920
That voice...!

00:16:22.920 --> 00:16:23.420
That way!

00:16:29.930 --> 00:16:32.020
Gothim?! Are you okay?

00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:34.510
We’ll save you!

00:16:46.780 --> 00:16:50.450
Why did it have to be
you people?!

00:16:50.450 --> 00:16:56.950
Yeah! I even bought RC cameras
to record some cool Inteleon footage!

00:16:56.950 --> 00:16:59.370
So those weird things were cameras!

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:04.460
But all we got shots of was you!
Don’t you know when to stop, meow?!

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:06.270
Huh? <i>You’re</i> the ones
who should stop!

00:17:06.270 --> 00:17:08.220
Don’t copy me, meow!

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:11.670
Aceburn, break this cage!

00:17:20.440 --> 00:17:23.790
Too bad.
It won’t break that easily!

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:26.800
Well, we’ve made it this far,
may as well pick up the loose charms.

00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:31.200
Pikachu and Aceburn...
And that little crybaby Pokémon while we’re at it.

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:35.440
We’ll present them all to Sakaki,
along with Inteleon, meow!

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:41.980
Messon!
Let ‘em see what you’ve learned!

00:17:42.710 --> 00:17:46.710
You’ve been thrown straight in the deep end,
but this is the start of your battle!

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:52.040
Hurry up and catch it!

00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:53.700
Get ready, meow!

00:17:54.850 --> 00:17:57.100
Messon! Aim straight up
and use Water Gun!

00:18:06.320 --> 00:18:07.420
It vanished!

00:18:09.140 --> 00:18:11.210
It soaked up its own Water Gun!

00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:13.320
Now your enemies can’t see you!

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:16.180
Relax and use Water Gun on Nyarth!

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:21.710
Even if you can’t see it,
you can guess where it is!

00:18:21.710 --> 00:18:23.370
Sonansu, around there!

00:18:27.110 --> 00:18:30.300
Quickly get out of there,
without a sound and without a trace!

00:18:32.560 --> 00:18:34.380
Now, Water Gun!

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:36.680
Then run for it, Messon!

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:38.090
Great job!

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:42.790
Attacking from a distance,
then running before it can be hit back!

00:18:42.790 --> 00:18:45.650
That’s Messon’s
hit-and-run battle style!

00:18:46.940 --> 00:18:49.350
That’s not fair!

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:53.320
Since it’s come to this...
You’ve forced our hand!

00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:57.910
What’s that?

00:19:08.170 --> 00:19:12.010
The device for when Inteleon vanishes
actually helped...!

00:19:12.010 --> 00:19:15.110
If we can see you,
the battle’s ours, meow!

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:18.350
Forget about the battle!
Run, Messon!

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:29.610
Messon!

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:31.730
We’ll catch you, meow!

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:45.100
It went back into its ball...

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:46.410
What was that?

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:48.500
A move called
“Dragonfly Turnaround”!

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:50.740
That’s great!

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:56.120
You did it, Messon!

00:19:56.120 --> 00:20:01.680
Hitting your opponent then returning,
you’ve learned the ultimate hit-and-run tactic!

00:20:03.140 --> 00:20:08.310
All right, Pikachu, Messon, Aceburn!
Let’s break down this cage together!

00:20:09.150 --> 00:20:10.870
Nyarth, are you okay?

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:13.360
Sonansu, snap out of it!

00:20:15.320 --> 00:20:17.400
Now the tables have turned!

00:20:18.260 --> 00:20:19.780
No way...

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:23.830
You can finish the job, Aceburn!
Pyro Ball!

00:20:23.830 --> 00:20:26.100
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:20:34.610 --> 00:20:37.400
<i>What an awful feeling!</i>

00:20:40.770 --> 00:20:43.670
Gothim! I was worried about you!

00:20:45.020 --> 00:20:47.520
We gave them a good beating!

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:51.030
Oh, this is it, this is it,
this is it, this is it, this is it!

00:20:51.530 --> 00:20:53.490
Messon, you were the star.

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:57.970
We rushed over,
but didn’t have to do a thing.

00:21:07.670 --> 00:21:09.750
Hey, Messon!

00:21:09.750 --> 00:21:11.280
Where are you?

00:21:12.760 --> 00:21:13.840
Hihidaruma?

00:21:26.520 --> 00:21:28.560
It was up there?

00:21:28.560 --> 00:21:30.600
Good job, Messon!

00:21:31.330 --> 00:21:36.200
Meeting someone to aspire towards
has given Messon a change of heart.

00:21:36.760 --> 00:21:42.210
Work hard with Go to hopefully reach that
lofty summit someday, Messon!

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:51.540
Pikachu!

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:52.410
Utsubot!

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:53.120
Transel!

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:53.920
